  "landfallEstimate": "To cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 13\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 02.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 13 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 2215 UTC OF 02.11.2026 BASED ON 2100 UTC\nOF 02.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] over Westcentral Bay of Bengal\nclose to South Andhra Pradesh Coast\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over Westcentral Bay of Bengal off South\nAndhra Pradesh Coast moved north-northwestwards with a speed of 9 kmph during past 6 hrs and lay\ncentered at 2100 UTC of today, the 02nd November, 2026 over the Westcentral Bay of Bengal close to\nSouth Andhra Pradesh Coast near Latitude 15.3\u00b0N and Longitude 80.3\u00b0E, about 30 km southeast of\nOngole (43221, Andhra Pradesh), 50 km northeast of Kavali (43243, Andhra Pradesh), 100 km north-\nnortheast of Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh), and 140 km southwest of Machilipatnam (43185, Andhra\nPradesh).\nLandfall process continues, the inner spiral band in the northern sector entered into the south Coastal\nAndhra Pradesh. Wall cloud region is entering into the land.\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards and cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a\nSevere Cyclonic Storm with wind speed of 100 to 110 kmph gusting to 120 kmph between Nellore (Andhra\nPradesh, 43245) and Narsapur (Andhra Pradesh, 43187), close to Ongole (Andhra Pradesh, 43221) during\nnext 3 hours.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at\nMachilipatnam.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n02.11.26/2100 15.3/80.3 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0000 15.5/80.2 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/79.9 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.3/79.8 65-75 gusting to 85 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1800 16.7/79.8 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n04.11.26/0600 17.4/79.9 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\nThe estimated central pressure is 994.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nNellore reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1009.4 hPa, 24 hours pressure change (P24) as -1.0\nhPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 2300/04kt, Kavali reported MSLP of 1007.3\nhPa, P24 as -3.6 hPa and MSW 2900/08kt, Bapatla reported MSLP of 1007.9 hPa, P24 as -2.6\nhPa and MSW 500/18kt, Ongole reported MSLP of 1003.0 hPa, P24 as -7.2 hPa and MSW\n3600/19kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 2100 UTC, Vortex (Murasu) over west-central bay off\nAndhra Pradesh coast and neighbourhood centered near 15.3N / 80.3E. Intensity",
